source: crates/standalone/fixture/src/lib.rs
---
Make organizations and manage who is in them.

\e[1mUsage\e[0m: \e[1m\e[36mink\e[0m \e[1m\e[36morg\e[0m \e[36m<COMMAND>\e[0m

\e[1mExamples\e[0m
  \e[1m\e[36mink\e[0m \e[1m\e[36morg\e[0m \e[1m\e[36mlist\e[0m  \e[2m# \e[0mYour organizations and your role in each

\e[1mCommands\e[0m
  \e[1m\e[36mcreate\e[0m  Make an organization, with you as its owner
  \e[1m\e[36mlist\e[0m    The organizations you are a member of
  \e[1m\e[36mmember\e[0m  Who is in an organization

\e[1mNotes\e[0m
  An organization owns sites and deploy keys of its own, so they outlive any
  member. Roles: owner (everything), admin (everything but destroying), writer
  (read, deploy, edit), reader (read). Run another command as an organization
  with `\e[1m\e[36m--org\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m<ID>\e[0m`.

\e[1mExit codes\e[0m
  0  Done
  2  Wrong usage: no API named, a key that is none, a private key that would
     print to a terminal
  3  No key, or the API refused the signature, or nobody approved the key in
     time
  4  The API could not be reached or failed; safe to retry

\e[1mEnvironment\e[0m
  \e[1m\e[36mINK_API\e[0m       The address of the API, as --api
  \e[1m\e[36mINK_SITE\e[0m      The site's id, as --site
  \e[1m\e[36mINK_KEY\e[0m       The private key to sign requests with, for a CI job; never a
                flag, so it stays out of process lists. `\e[1m\e[36mink\e[0m \e[1m\e[36mlogin\e[0m` keeps one in
                the config folder instead
  \e[1m\e[36mINK_KEY_FILE\e[0m  A file that holds that key, in place of INK_KEY

\e[2mSee also\e[0m  \e[1m\e[36mink key\e[0m, \e[1m\e[36mink whoami\e[0m
\e[2mDocs\e[0m      \e[34mhttps://github.com/uses-ink/uses.ink/blob/main/docs/cli.md\e[0m
\e[2mGlobal\e[0m    \e[1m\e[36m-C,\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m--json,\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m-q,\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m-v,\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m--color,\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m--no-progress,\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m--log,\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m--log-file\e[0m
          \e[2m(see `ink --help`)\e[0m
